# A mark must never be the thing standing in front of what it proves, and the
# body must read in every pose (docs/ART.md §5, §7). Every frame here is at PLAY
# zoom, because that is the only size that counts: a mark that only behaves in a
# close shot is not fixed.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/marks.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --fit=scanner_lens,boots_magnet,mod_spring,glide_wing
# Each pair is a control frame and then the mark, from the same place, so what
# the mark added to the picture can be counted and not argued about.
coast calm

# --- A blow leaves the machine standing there --------------------------------
# Shot on the first frame after the blow, inside the flash: the struck plate is
# paper, the rest of the body is still its own violet, and its lens is still
# amber. (The flash is 60 ms; a `wait` here would shoot after it.)
place pinewood
wait 1.0
spawn watcher
wait 1.2
shot 01-before-the-blow with mob:watcher
try 16
walkto part 1.6
tap swing
await hit 1.8
end
shot 02-the-blow-leaves-it-standing with mob:watcher
# And once more at the zoom the art review shot it at, where the old flash was a
# bone-white silhouette sixty pixels tall with the amber gone out of it.
zoom 8
wait 0.4
try 16
walkto part 1.6
tap swing
await hit 1.8
end
shot 03-and-close-enough-to-count-the-pixels with mob:watcher
zoom 15
wait 0.4

# --- The machine's own light is smaller than the machine ----------------------
# Its working part at night, at the distance it is read from: a ring of loose
# amber pixels round the part, never a disc wider than the body wearing it.
coast calm
wait 0.4
place coast
hour 22
weather clear:0
wait 1.2
spawn watcher
wait 1.6
shot 04-its-light-is-smaller-than-it-is with mob:watcher

# --- A read through a stolen lens, over the thing it reads --------------------
tap ability_scan
await ability:scan 5
wait 0.4
shot 05-read-over-the-thing-it-reads with mob:watcher

# --- The dash leaves the body showing ----------------------------------------
# Speed lines are ink over the world, laid where the body WAS: the player must
# still be a person at the head of them.
coast calm
wait 0.5
hour 11
weather clear:0
place coast
wait 1.4
shot 06-before-the-dash with land:coast
tap ability_dash
await ability:dash 5
wait 0.03
shot 07-the-dash-leaves-the-body-showing with land:coast

# --- The magnet line is a line -----------------------------------------------
# Far enough back that the line is a LINE: a magnet throw reaches eight tiles,
# and a rope proven at arm's length proves nothing.
# Back off until the tip is nearly out of throw, then step in until it catches:
# a magnet line reaches eight tiles, and a rope proven at arm's length proves
# nothing about whether a player can see it.
place tip
wait 0.8
walk -1,-1 2.6
wait 0.3
shot 08-across-from-a-tip with prop:tip
try 8
walk 1,1 0.3
tap ability_grapple
await ability:grapple 1.5
end
shot 09-the-line-takes-hold with prop:tip
wait 0.45
shot 10-and-it-shortens with prop:tip

# --- Crouched, still a person ------------------------------------------------
coast calm
wait 0.4
ground heath
wait 1.0
shot 11-standing-in-the-heather
hold crouch
await crouched 3
wait 0.6
shot 12-down-in-the-heather with crouched
walk 1,0 0.5
shot 13-and-moving-down-there with crouched
# And closer than anyone plays, which is where the art review found it: the
# pose has to hold up under a magnifying glass as well as at 640x360.
zoom 6
wait 0.5
shot 14-down-in-the-heather-close with crouched
release crouch
wait 0.5
shot 15-and-up-again-close
zoom 15
wait 0.4

# --- A read holds through a throw and through a flight ------------------------
# A scan lays a bracket on every working part for six seconds. It used to drop
# the WHOLE read -- brackets and the tell over a machine that has noticed you --
# the moment anything moved the body, so a glide went blind for all six of its
# seconds, which is exactly when a player wants to know who is looking. Now only
# a throw holds back the next brackets, so two ability marks never land on the
# same thirty pixels, and nothing at all holds back the tell. What a player sees
# is one unbroken read.
coast calm
wait 0.5
place coast
hour 11
weather clear:0
wait 1.2
spawn watcher
wait 1.4
tap ability_scan
await ability:scan 5
wait 0.5
shot 16-the-read-is-laid with mob:watcher
tap ability_dash
await ability:dash 4
wait 0.04
shot 17-and-holds-through-the-throw with mob:watcher
wait 0.7
shot 18-and-is-still-there-after with mob:watcher
# And through the six seconds of a glide, which is a flight and not a throw:
# off a height with a machine still in reach, the read is on it the whole way.
place summit
zoom 11
wait 1.4
walk 1,1 1.6
spawn lineman
# The lens is on a nine-second cooldown and `await ability:scan` only says it
# has ever fired, so the wait is the real gate here: without it the second tap
# is refused and the frames below prove nothing at all.
wait 9.0
tap ability_scan
await ability:scan 5
wait 0.4
shot 19-a-machine-read-on-a-height with mob:lineman
tap ability_glide
await gliding 5
wait 0.8
shot 20-and-through-a-whole-glide with gliding,mob:lineman

# --- Breath steps off the snow -----------------------------------------------
# The cue fires on its own beat and hangs a second and a half, so the frame is
# taken right after the cold is first felt (the first cue is due at once) and
# again a beat later: breath has to be visible on white ground in both.
place snowfield
hour 19
weather clear:0
wait 1.6
await cold 12
await pressure_bites 15
await breath 10
wait 0.15
shot 21-breath-on-white-ground with cold,land:snowfield
wait 2.0
await breath 10
wait 0.6
shot 22-and-the-next-breath with cold,land:snowfield
# And at night, on the same white ground. A mark's paint is as pale as snow is,
# so under one light the two land on the same value and the cloud vanishes into
# the field it was breathed over: a breath has to step off its page at every
# hour, not only while the sun is up.
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 1.6
await cold 12
await breath 12
wait 0.15
shot 23-breath-on-white-ground-at-night with cold,land:snowfield
